---
import DefaultPageLayout from "../../layouts/DefaultPageLayout.astro";
import Petapetual from "../../components/Petapetual.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
---

<DefaultPageLayout
    title="For Living Abroad"
    description="Just because you aren't in the same country as your loved one's final resting place doesn't mean you have to miss out on paying your respects. Access your Petapetual memorial no matter where you are in the world."
>
    <article class="article-container">
        <a href="/examples" class="back-link">
            <i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> All Use Cases
        </a>

        <Image
            src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1548227725-0141254f3369?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxwaG90by1wYWdlfHx8fGVufDB8fHx8fA%3D%3D&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80&w=2070"
            alt="Distance makes loss hurt hard and paying respects harder. Petapetual's online memorials aim to help those who live abroad feel more connected to their lost ones."
            class="article-hero"
            width="2070"
            height="400"
        />

        <h1 class="article-title">
            <Petapetual /> for those living overseas
        </h1>

        <p class="article-text">
            Are you living far away from your loved one's final resting place?
            Perhaps you are studying or working abroad and now find yourself
            separated from your hometown and family? In such cases, it is hard
            to show up and pay respects at a physical cemetery, temple, or
            columbarium.
        </p>

        <p class="article-text">
            <Petapetual /> bridges the distance, bringing you closer to those you've
            lost. Pay your respects from anywhere in the world, as if you were right
            there beside them.
        </p>

        <h2 class="article-subtitle">Always in reach</h2>

        <p class="article-text">
            Once set up, a <Petapetual /> memorial is always accessible to you, no
            matter where in the world you are. Across mobile, tablet, and desktop:
            no app installations are required. Simply sign in whenever you want to,
            or whenever you miss the dearly departed and visit their <a
                href="/how-it-works"
                class="article-link">virtual memorial</a
            >.
        </p>

        <h2 class="article-subtitle">Invite others to your memorial</h2>

        <p class="article-text">
            You don't have to pay your respects alone: invite other people to
            your memorials so you can all remember your late loved ones
            together: write loving messages in the guestbook, place <a
                href="/how-it-works#tributes"
                class="article-link">tributes</a
            >, and reminisce with one another across oceans and time zones.
        </p>

        <div class="article-cta">
            <a href="https://app.petapetual.com" class="cta-btn">
                Create a Memorial <i class="fas fa-arrow-right ml-1"></i>
            </a>
        </div>
    </article>
</DefaultPageLayout>

<style>
    @reference "tailwindcss";

    .article-container {
        @apply flex flex-col gap-6;
    }

    .back-link {
        @apply text-sm no-underline transition-colors;
        color: var(--color-pp-mid);
    }

    .back-link:hover {
        color: var(--color-pp-primary);
    }

    .article-hero {
        @apply w-full h-48 object-cover rounded-xl shadow-sm;
        @apply lg:h-72;
    }

    .article-title {
        @apply text-2xl font-bold;
        @apply lg:text-3xl;
        color: var(--color-pp-primary);
    }

    .article-subtitle {
        @apply text-xl font-semibold mt-2;
        color: var(--color-pp-primary);
    }

    .article-text {
        @apply leading-relaxed;
        color: var(--color-pp-dark);
    }

    .article-link {
        @apply underline transition-colors;
        color: var(--color-pp-primary);
        text-decoration-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-pp-primary) 50%, transparent);
    }

    .article-link:hover {
        text-decoration-color: var(--color-pp-primary);
    }

    .article-cta {
        @apply mt-4 py-8 text-center;
        border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-pp-mid) 30%, transparent);
    }

    .cta-btn {
        @apply inline-block px-6 py-3 rounded-lg font-semibold no-underline transition-colors;
        background-color: var(--color-pp-primary);
        color: var(--color-pp-light);
    }

    .cta-btn:hover {
        opacity: 0.9;
    }
</style>
